  "query_preview": "..Today through Thursday...Drier air sets in today \nacross northern Arizona behind the departing low. Zonal flow sets \nin across much of Arizona through at least the middle of this \nweek, keeping dry conditions and gradually warming temperatures in\nstore for the region. Winds look to mainly be light and variable \nto start, gradually tending south/southwestward through the week.\n\nFriday onward...A deepening trough over the northwest, and a strong \nsub-tropical jet over the Pacific will help increase moisture \nadvection into Arizona by the end of the week. Precipitation looks \nto being late Friday and then continue into Sunday. As the trough \nbegins to dig and the jet becomes further enhanced, deeper moisture \nlooks to move into the region on Sunday. \n\nUncertainty remains in the exact setup going into the end of the \nweek, thus confidence in any specific details remains low. As of now \nthe latest operational ECMWF seems to favor a wetter solution with a \nstronger sub-tropical jet, while the GFS favors a weaker and faster \njet and therefore lighter QPF amounts. Looking at the ensemble \nguidance, most of the EPS and CMCE members favor the wetter ECMWF \nsolution while the GEFS members mostly lean towards the drier GFS \nsolution. This leans towards the wetter solution being more likely, \nhowever with some model disagreement confidence will remain low. \nNevertheless, a return of cooler and more unsettled conditions look \nto set in by the end of the week.",
